in (serve CLI entry)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/web/serve.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "web_serve_env_over_flag_precedence", "label": "env > --flag > default config precedence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/web/serve.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A container/VM has no shell to pass --port to, so each of PORT/HOST/GAME_PIN/SAVES_DIR has a pure resolve*() with env precedence and a safe fallback. GAME_PIN matters most: a freshly generated per-boot PIN is useless once a host can restart the process without the owner watching the console."}, {"id": "web_serve_pin_not_echoed_when_from_env", "label": "An operator-supplied PIN is never echoed to the console", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/web/serve.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A generated PIN exists nowhere else so the console is the only place to learn it; a GAME_PIN was chosen by its operator and printing it copies a password into journald/`docker logs` for every boot in the retention window."}, {"id": "web_serve_sse_over_websocket", "label": "Plain http + SSE instead of WebSockets", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/web/serve.ts", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Node's stdlib has `http` but no WS server and this project takes no new dependencies; SSE covers a turn-based game fine and gives reconnect-on-drop for free via the browser's EventSource -- exactly what a phone needs across screen locks and network blips."}], "edges": [{"source": "web_serve_main", "target": "web_serve_parseargs", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "src/web/serve.ts", "source_location"